{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Path Traversal in algo-httpserv"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Versions of `algo-httpserv` prior to 1.1.2 are vulnerable to Path Traversal.  Due to insufficient input sanitization, attackers can access server files by using relative paths. \n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.2 or later."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: algo-httpserv\nFixed Version: 1.1.2\nLink: [GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp)\nVersions of `algo-httpserv` prior to 1.1.2 are vulnerable to Path Traversal.  Due to insufficient input sanitization, attackers can access server files by using relative paths. \n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.2 or later.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|algo-httpserv|1.1.2|[GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgjv-rghq-qhgp)|\n\nVersions of `algo-httpserv` prior to 1.1.2 are vulnerable to Path Traversal.  Due to insufficient input sanitization, attackers can access server files by using relative paths. \n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.2 or later."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.6,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.6",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-43138",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "async: Prototype Pollution in async"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In Async before 2.6.4 and 3.x before 3.2.2, a malicious user can obtain privileges via the mapValues() method, aka lib/internal/iterator.js createObjectIterator prototype pollution."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-43138",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-43138\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: async\nFixed Version: 3.2.2, 2.6.4\nLink: [CVE-2021-43138](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-43138)\nIn Async before 2.6.4 and 3.x before 3.2.2, a malicious user can obtain privileges via the mapValues() method, aka lib/internal/iterator.js createObjectIterator prototype pollution.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-43138**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|async|3.2.2, 2.6.4|[CVE-2021-43138](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2021-43138)|\n\nIn Async before 2.6.4 and 3.x before 3.2.2, a malicious user can obtain privileges via the mapValues() method, aka lib/internal/iterator.js createObjectIterator prototype pollution."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
